WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.939
If you're new to the adventures of Wonder
Woman, you might not be familiar with the

00:00:03.939 --> 00:00:07.830
villain known as Cheetah — but now that
she's ready to hit the silver screen, there's

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.460
no better time to bone up on Diana's feline
arch-nemesis.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.460
This is the untold truth of Cheetah.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.030
Barbara Ann Minerva has been the main Cheetah
in the comics ever since the 1980s, and is

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.110
easily the character's most well-known alter
ego.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.320
And she's also the character Kristen Wiig
plays in Wonder Woman 1984.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.320
"I don't wanna be like anyone.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.670
I wanna be an apex predator."

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.239
But she wasn't the first Cheetah.

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:40.760
While Minerva first appeared in 1987, another
Cheetah debuted in 1943, only a couple of

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.839
years after Wonder Woman herself.

00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:45.030
That very first Cheetah was Priscilla Rich.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:50.109
She debuted in Wonder Woman Vol. 1 #6, by
the comic's original creative team of William

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:52.469
Marston and Harry G. Peter.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:59.129
Priscilla was the one and only Cheetah until
1980, when Wonder Woman Vol. 1 #274 saw the

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:04.159
mantle taken up by Priscilla's niece, an environmental
activist named Deborah Domaine.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:09.680
The DC continuity was rebooted in the "Crisis
on Infinite Earths" event in the mid-1980s,

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:15.400
leaving the door open for another new Cheetah
in Wonder Woman Vol. 2 #7: Barbara Ann Minerva

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.400
herself.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.600
A man named Sebastian Ballesteros usurped
Minerva's powers and briefly became the Cheetah

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.710
in Wonder Woman Vol. 2 #171, but Barbara returned
to the role before long.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.630
Given that Wonder Woman stands shoulder-to-shoulder
with Superman and has been known to fight

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:37.890
Greek gods from time to time, you'd think
her arch-nemesis would be comparably powerful.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.729
But Priscilla Rich, the original Cheetah,
had no superpowers at all.

00:01:41.729 --> 00:01:46.749
In fact, much like a certain other DC character,
Priscilla's primary asset is her wealth.

00:01:46.749 --> 00:01:51.540
Her villainous origin lies in the moment Wonder
Woman steals the spotlight from her at a charity

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.649
event, making the young heiress intensely
jealous.

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:59.240
As any reasonable person would, Priscilla
responds to this unintentional slight by putting

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:04.689
on a cheetah skin costume and framing Wonder
Woman for robbery, then trying to kill her.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:09.030
Despite her relatively low power level, Cheetah
remained a thorn in Wonder Woman's side throughout

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.520
the 1940s.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:15.410
During one story, she betrays her own country
by passing on military secrets to the Japanese

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:16.820
during World War II.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.250
In another, Priscilla infiltrates Paradise
Island and steals Queen Hippolyta's magical

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.030
girdle of power, enabling her to finally go
toe-to-toe with Wonder Woman herself.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:30.060
Obviously, she still loses — which really
can't be good for the ol' self-esteem.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.380
One element of the Cheetah character that's
been there since the very beginning is the

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.930
notion of the feline persona as a separate
personality.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:42.080
Cheetah's human alter ego, whoever that may
be, often struggles against and gives in to

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.100
the feral persona in their head.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.700
Before Priscilla Rich starts wearing her rug,
a fully outfitted Cheetah appears in her vanity

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.700
mirror, encouraging the heiress to give in
to her hatred of Wonder Woman — and become

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.870
the, quote, "treacherous, relentless huntress"
she already is on the inside.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.640
Decades later, Debbie Domaine stepped into
the Cheetah's furry shoes.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.430
Debbie is a genuinely nice person and a good
friend to Wonder Woman — until she's brainwashed

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:10.120
by the international supervillain Kobra, who
transforms her into a vicious huntress in

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.120
her own right.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.970
For Barbara Ann Minerva, the divide is more
mystical, with the animal instincts of the

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:19.850
Cheetah leading her down a path of animalistic
viciousness that part of her finds repellent.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:24.350
No matter how much she might struggle, however,
the Cheetah within her always yearns to be

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.350
free.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.230
Given her semi-feral nature, it might come
as some surprise to find that Cheetah is actually

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.920
something of a joiner.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.520
Priscilla Rich, for example, is a founding
member of Villainy Incorporated, an all-female

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.010
team formed to take revenge on Wonder Woman.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:44.770
Debuting in Wonder Woman Vol. 1 #28, the team
made several appearances over the years, hoping

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:47.940
to find strength in numbers against the powerful
Amazon princess.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.700
Naturally, it never quite works out for them.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.120
In addition to initially being an agent of
Kobra, Debbie Domaine is later recruited by

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.400
the Ultra-Humanite into the Secret Society
of Super-Villains, DC's premiere villain team

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.730
of the 1970s and '80s.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:07.690
As a member of the Secret Society, Debbie
faces both the Justice Society and the Justice

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:08.690
League.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:12.770
Then you've got Barbara Ann Minerva, who is
a founding member of the post-Crisis version

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:17.359
of the Injustice League, which debuted in
the Justice League of America Wedding Special.

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:21.940
She's part of the triumvirate that leads the
League alongside Lex Luthor and the Joker,

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:26.650
mirroring the much-celebrated "DC Trinity"
of their respective arch-enemies.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:31.220
Cheetah has also been part of what might be
DC's most enduring supervillain team of all,

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.660
the Legion of Doom.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.550
But that team's first appearance wasn't actually
in a comic book.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:42.120
In 1978, the children's cartoon series Super
Friends was retooled as Challenge of the Super

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.040
Friends, bringing it closer to the comics
it was based on.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:50.340
Challenge expanded the show's roster of heroes,
and introduced a team of DC Comics supervillains

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.310
for them to square off against each week.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.900
The Legion of Doom, a creation of this cartoon,
is brought together by Lex Luthor in a flying

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.570
saucer-esque swamp lair.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:04.430
"It is the purpose of the Legion to align
our infamous forces against the powers of

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:09.811
good and defeat them, leaving us the rulers
of the world."

00:05:09.811 --> 00:05:14.970
The Priscilla Rich version of Cheetah represents
Wonder Woman's rogues gallery, alongside Giganta,

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.970
another animal print-clad Golden Age villainess.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:22.160
Cheetah's most memorable episode in the series
is "The Secret Origins of the Super Friends,"

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.100
in which the Legionnaires travel back in time
to prevent their enemies from becoming superheroes.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:31.370
Cheetah disguises herself as an Amazon and
competes in the contest to determine who will

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:36.150
become Wonder Woman, managing to defeat Princess
Diana and become Wonder Woman herself.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:41.030
Her triumph is short-lived however, as the
Flash also travels back in time to set things

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.030
right.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.810
While there have technically been four Cheetahs,
the honest truth is that there are only two

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.890
of real significance to the comics.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:51.680
But it's still worth taking a moment to find
out more about the also-rans.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.080
Debbie Domaine is Priscilla Rich's niece,
and heir to her fortune.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.830
Ambivalent about her own wealth, Debbie becomes
an ecological activist, and even makes friends

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:03.260
with Wonder Woman after encountering the Amazon
at sea.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:08.200
Unfortunately, she's soon kidnapped by agents
of Kobra, and a regimen of torture and brainwashing

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.139
turns her into an agent of evil.

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:14.400
She never appeared in a Wonder Woman story
after her introduction, although she did turn

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.560
up as a villain in various other stories published
over the next few years, including "Crisis

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.919
on Infinite Earths" — the story that would
ultimately erase her from continuity.

00:06:23.919 --> 00:06:29.200
Sebastian Ballesteros is an Argentine businessman
and lover of another Wonder Woman foe, the

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.770
immortal sorceress Circe.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:36.760
In a 2001 storyline, he is able to convince
Urzkartaga, the god who empowers Cheetah,

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:41.300
to take the Cheetah's powers from Barbara
Ann Minerva and give them to him instead.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.450
Sebastian is ultimately no match for Barbara
Ann, however.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:48.790
Unable to access the Cheetah's powers, she
instead steals the powers of one of the Furies

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:54.540
of Greek myth, and ultimately kills Ballesteros,
giving his blood to Urzkartaga as an offering,

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.620
in exchange for becoming Cheetah once more.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:02.520
When Barbara Ann Minerva was first introduced
in 1987, she was depicted as a duplicitous

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:07.420
woman who feigns friendship with Wonder Woman
in an attempt to steal her magic lasso.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:13.090
When DC revised Wonder Woman's continuity
in 2016 as part of DC Rebirth, however, she

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.520
was made into a far more likable character.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:20.460
They also tied her origin more closely to
Wonder Woman's, cementing them as fated arch-nemeses.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:26.020
In the current continuity, Barbara Ann Minerva
is a brilliant archaeologist with an impressive

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:27.070
reputation.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:31.650
When an Amazon princess shows up in the US
speaking what appears to be a dialect of ancient

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.570
Greek, Dr. Minerva is called on to help translate.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:39.320
Thus, Barbara Ann actually teaches Diana the
English language, and the two become close

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:40.320
friends.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.430
Unfortunately, their friendship is doomed
from the beginning — and Minerva is soon

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.800
led down a very dark path indeed.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.240
Just as Wonder Woman can trace the origin
of her powers to the gods and goddesses of

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.510
Mount Olympus, her nemesis is also empowered
by an ancient deity.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:58.540
Cheetah's powers come from an African plant
god named Urzkartaga, and they're as much

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.360
of a curse as they are a blessing.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:04.729
During her travels, Barbara Ann Minerva learns
of a ritual by which a human woman can become

00:08:04.729 --> 00:08:07.740
a bride of Urzkartaga, thus attaining great
power.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:11.800
She attempts the ritual, having learned from
her friendship with Wonder Woman that god-given

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.199
superpowers are a very real thing.

00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:19.260
Unfortunately, what Minerva doesn't take into
account is that ancient gods tend to be narrow-minded

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:20.510
and kinda sexist.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:25.520
So, because she isn't a virgin, the god rejects
her, and with his rejection comes a horrific

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:30.570
curse — transforming Barbara Ann into a
bestial creature who craves human flesh.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:35.680
Ultimately, Barbara Ann Minerva does gain
great power from Urzkartaga, despite the drawbacks.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:40.759
Her speed, strength, agility, and vicious
killer instincts make her a formidable foe,

00:08:40.759 --> 00:08:42.629
even for someone like Wonder Woman.

00:08:43.629 --> 00:08:47.959
In reality, Barbara Ann Minerva's transformation
is ultimately the fault of another Wonder

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:50.421
Woman villain: The business tycoon known as
Veronica Cale.

00:08:50.421 --> 00:08:55.791
Cale was introduced to DC Comics in 2003,
in an effort to give Wonder Woman her own

00:08:55.791 --> 00:08:56.949
Lex Luthor.

00:08:56.949 --> 00:09:02.279
Since first appearing in Wonder Woman Vol.
2 #196, she's become one of Wonder Woman's

00:09:02.279 --> 00:09:03.360
greatest foes.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:08.360
Cale is rich, successful, extremely intelligent,
and resents everything Wonder Woman stands

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.360
for.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.279
And it's Veronica Cale who sends Barbara Ann
Minerva on her expedition to gain the powers

00:09:13.279 --> 00:09:18.149
of Urzkartaga, hoping that an empowered Minerva
might be able to help Cale find Wonder Woman's

00:09:18.149 --> 00:09:20.040
homeland of Themyscira.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:24.350
Wonder Woman had previously promised to help
Barbara Ann if she ran into trouble, but Cale

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:28.190
disrupts their lines of communication and
keeps Wonder Woman too busy to check on her

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:30.300
friend — until it's too late.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:35.240
Unaware of the extent of Cale's manipulation,
Cheetah blames Wonder Woman for her transformation

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.779
into a bloodthirsty beast.

00:09:36.779 --> 00:09:40.890
Although Barbara Ann occasionally regains
her humanity over the years and ultimately

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:44.920
understands that Veronica Cale is to blame
for her predicament, she and Wonder Woman

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.079
remain enemies.

00:09:47.079 --> 00:09:50.980
In the convoluted history of comic book characters,
it seems like everyone has hooked up with

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:55.369
everyone else, and a prime example of this
is the fling between Clark Kent and Barbara

00:09:55.369 --> 00:09:58.699
Ann Minerva fling from the non-canon comic
Superman: American Alien.

00:09:58.699 --> 00:10:04.059
In this story, not only does the pre-Supes
Clark Kent have a romantic tryst with Barbara,

00:10:04.059 --> 00:10:06.940
but she also helps him establish his dual
identity.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.949
The premise for this comic is that Clark Kent
wins a trip to the Bahamas, but his plane

00:10:10.949 --> 00:10:12.089
crashes on the way.

00:10:12.089 --> 00:10:16.110
Luckily, he finds his way to Bruce Wayne's
yacht, but the billionaire isn't there.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:20.160
Naturally, everyone assumes that Clark is
Bruce Wayne, and Barbara Ann, another guest

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.660
on the yacht, convinces him to go along with
it.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.790
Clark and Barbara open up quite a bit to one
another throughout the storyline, with Clark

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:30.980
even dancing around the idea of sharing his
true, alien origin with her.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:34.980
Eventually, the two part ways with nothing
more than fond memories of one another — but

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.480
it's still a fascinating look at two characters
who "might have been."

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:43.019
If you're discussing which DC Comics characters
are the fastest of all, Superman and the Flash

00:10:43.019 --> 00:10:44.819
tend to be the main focus.

00:10:44.819 --> 00:10:47.519
"That feels like an oversimplification."

00:10:47.519 --> 00:10:51.839
Cheetah's name rarely even comes up — but
honestly, it probably should.

00:10:51.839 --> 00:10:57.139
During the "Flash War" comics storyline, longtime
Flash writer Josh Williamson gave DC Nation

00:10:57.139 --> 00:11:00.050
his list of the ten fastest DC characters.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:05.439
The first three are all versions of the Flash:
Barry Allen, Wally West, and the Reverse Flash.

00:11:05.439 --> 00:11:07.300
Superman comes in fourth, naturally.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:12.839
In fifth place is the Black Racer, a swift-moving
and inescapable incarnation of Death.

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:14.119
And sixth on the list?

00:11:14.119 --> 00:11:16.819
Barbara Ann Minerva, the fleet-footed Cheetah.

00:11:16.819 --> 00:11:22.029
That puts her ahead of Wonder Woman, Shazam,
and basically everybody else in the DC Universe.

00:11:22.029 --> 00:11:26.509
It also means she's almost as fast as Death
itself, which you have to imagine is something

00:11:26.509 --> 00:11:28.809
Barbara Ann is pretty proud of.

00:11:28.809 --> 00:11:33.079
Empowered by a god and given the aspect of
the fastest animal on land, Cheetah's speed

00:11:33.079 --> 00:11:35.059
really is no joke.

